tasks.brief:
Third attempt at T-0218. T-0226 timed out (90 min, no report). T-0231 landed only stage A and was cut off while its first build was running. Its report (docs/reviews/2026-11-11-fix-pdm-4ch-T-0231.md) is unfinished, with an empty fix block. Start from what is on main. Do NOT redo stage A.

Owner's ruling (Q-0070, decision 172, amends 166), verbatim: "Option 3 + option 2. Signal vias (not tracks) may pass through VS-In2; each pour must stay one island and keep >= 95 % of its area. Also allow a placement stage that gives the U1 transistor/resistor block (Q3-Q6, R17-R24/R50/R51) and the channel signal columns room. Recheck the heat budget (decision 9) after the change. No corridor notch. The scripts gate (question 4) is already settled by decision 163."

Sources:
- docs/reviews/2026-11-11-fix-pdm-4ch-T-0211-rejected.md: the 78 open items, by group (west 27, U1 strip/analog 47, J3 4);
- docs/reviews/2026-11-11-fix-pdm-4ch-T-0231.md;
- design-notes 8.16/8.17. The 8.18 that the T-0211 report cites never landed, so write your notes as a new 8.18;
- hardware/pdm-4ch/STATUS.md.

Method: decision 163. Fixes go into hardware/pdm-4ch/scripts/, and the board is the build output. Placement moves use tools/kpcb.py.

State on main:
- routing_build.py has VIA_OK_POURS = {'VS-In2'}: pour-VS-In2 is SetDoNotAllowVias(False), and it is exported as a wire_keepout;
- fixed_routes.py has POUR_LOSS_MAX = 0.05;
- the VS-In2 baseline is 1 island, 1190.7 mm2;
- the board is the T-0210 build: 0 errors, 78 unconnected, parity 0.
First, confirm with git log and grep that these lines are there.

REPORT DISCIPLINE (this is what failed last time):
- Write the report within the first 10 minutes.
- From the start, its fix block lists T-0218 under 'blocked' (door two-way, reason 'in progress: <stage>').
- Update it after each stage.
- Move T-0218 to 'done' only at 0 unconnected.
- Never leave done and blocked both empty.

TIME BOX:
- 1 run per build (build_routing.sh 1 25). Parallel runs were identical (T-0211).
- A normal build takes about 5 min (T-0209). Start each build in the background with a 20-min limit.
- If the via-freedom build has not ended by then, stop it and retry once with fewer passes (build_routing.sh 1 10). If that also hangs, report it as blocked (two-way: 'Freerouting does not converge with vias allowed in VS-In2') and go on to stage B, using the scripts as they are.
- At most 4 builds in total.
- Stop work at about 70 minutes. Land the best clean state, and finish the report.

STAGE A' – build with the via freedom (the change is already on main):
1. Run build_routing.sh 1 25.
2. The acceptance rules are unchanged (decision 166 as amended by 172): 0 DRC errors, parity 0, every pour at its baseline island count and >= 95 % of its baseline area, and fewer unconnected items than the board.
3. If the build is better: commit the board and run python3 tools/land.py.
4. Record the VS-In2 area and the island count before and after.

STAGE B – placement (option 2), then build and land:
1. Move the U1 transistor/resistor block (Q3-Q6, R17-R24, R50, R51) and the channel signal-column parts toward U1 and away from the VS/OUT outlines. The channel signal-column parts are those on DEN, SW_IN1-4, +3V3 (D102/D202/D402), IO0/2/3/5, EN, NTC, U12/U14-IS and R60.
2. Space the analog block so the U1 strip legs and the short links get lanes.
3. Constraints:
   - all SMT on top (decision 122);
   - nothing in a hole keep-out, the antenna strip or the CAN barrier;
   - everything inside the outline;
   - do not move the PROFETs, Q30/U30/D31, the connectors, the buck or U1;
   - change no power-zone outline.
4. If a move leaves a locked link or a fixed route dangling, fix it in scripts/fixed_routes.py.
5. Build with 1 run. Land if the build is better.

STAGE C – only if time is left:
- add fixed routes in fixed_routes.py for what the router leaves, using vias through VS-In2;
- for example J3 VBUS A4/A9/B4/B9 -> F2.1 on In2 (no via may sit in OUT1-B, decision 170);
- add GND ties for the leftover GND F.Cu islands.

After the last landed build:
1. Run python3 tools/heat_budget.py at 40 C (decision 9; pdm-4ch defaults, 4 x 4 A).
2. Report Tj. heat_budget.py does not model the In2 area. So state that the RthJA estimate is unchanged, provided every PROFET thermal via is still in VS-In2 and the VS-In2 loss is <= 5 %.
3. Update STATUS.md (the T-0231 'in progress' state is stale) and design-notes (new 8.18).

Checks: python3 tools/fix_check.py --role pcb-fixer --scope pdm-4ch:
- schematic unchanged;
- parity 0, 0 DRC errors;
- outline and holes unchanged;
- no bottom SMT.

If items stay unconnected at the end, list them under 'blocked' (two-way), with the exact nets and the next step (more room, or a named fixed route), so they come back as a follow-up.

ONE-WAY DOORS (stop and ask in the report, do not do):
- a corridor or notch in any power pour, a change to a power-zone outline, or a pour split;
- more than 5 % area loss;
- a signal track (not a via) on VS-In2;
- a via through any other power pour;
- moving a PROFET, Q30, a connector, a hole or the outline;
- a bottom-side part;
- a schematic change;
- a heat-budget Tj above the limit.
